  data: {
    LLM: "In negative rounds, hold onto your small cards (2s, 3s) to ensure you can stay under high cards played by opponents.\n\nContract Selection: If you have a balanced hand with no long suits, play your 'No Tricks' negative contract early. Save your 'Trumps' positive contract for when you hold an Ace and many cards of one suit.\n\nBleeding the King: If playing 'No King of Hearts,' lead small Hearts early to force the King out while you still have a low card to play underneath it.",
